      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(durable): add durable session task runtime foundation",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThis PR adds the opt-in, local-first durable runtime foundation proposed by PR1. The target failure mode is coordinator silence: long-running session/task/subagent work can continue across many steps, branches, and process restarts, but operators and runtime code need a bounded durable projection of which run, step, child, signal, or recovery state is open.\n\nThis is not a general-purpose workflow engine and does not include Work module, Workboard UI/tools, Task Flow projection adapters, or product-specific logic.\n\n## Dependency Chain\n\nThis is PR2 in the replacement durable runtime stack:\n\n1. PR1: durable session/task runtime RFC v2.\n2. PR2: durable runtime foundation, this PR.\n3. PR3: agent/session/subagent wiring on top of this foundation.\n\nThis PR is designed to be reviewable independently as a core foundation slice.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds:\n\n- `durable_runtime_*` tables in the shared OpenClaw state DB;\n- SQLite store lifecycle with schema version checks and shared state permission hardening;\n- runtime runs, steps, events, refs, links, timers, and signals;\n- local-first claim/release, heartbeat, recovery, and bounded worker helpers;\n- read-only CLI and Gateway inspection surfaces;\n- generic coordination projection with unsupported write controls disabled;\n- public `packages/gateway-protocol` schemas, inferred types, lazy validators, and validator tests for `durable.coordination.get`;\n- Kysely generated types and guardrails for the new schema;\n- public CLI docs for enablement, env vars, storage, and input retention.\n\n## Explicit Non-Scope\n\n- Work module behavior.\n- Workboard UI/tools.\n- Task Flow projection adapters.\n- Retention/compaction policy.\n- Postgres/multi-worker lease contention.\n- Automatic retry/resume policy.\n- Ledger-only write controls.\n\n## Latest Reviewer Follow-Up\n\nUpdated on 2026-07-03 after the latest ClawSweeper P1/P2 findings and proof refresh.\n\nHead: `cb0a5b5a9b0bcb46cd2f15469fd63c4db68d3358`.\n\nAddressed ClawSweeper findings:\n\n- Gateway startup still records the durable startup marker when `OPENCLAW_DURABLE_RUNTIME=1`, but agent-turn/chat-send/subagent mark-lost reconciliation now runs only with explicit `OPENCLAW_DURABLE_WORKER=1`.\n- `durable.coordination.get` now has public protocol params/result/projection schemas, inferred exported types, lazy validators, and validator tests.\n- The Gateway durable handler now uses `validateDurableCoordinationGetParams` and rejects invalid params before opening durable state.\n- Earlier disabled CLI, future-schema, and recovery-worker findings remain fixed: disabled inspection does not create or migrate shared state; unsupported newer durable schema versions are rejected before durable table DDL/ALTER/backfill; `OPENCLAW_DURABLE_RUNTIME=1` alone does not start reconciliation.\n\nRegression coverage added:\n\n- `src/durable/startup.test.ts` verifies runtime-enabled startup without the worker flag preserves running runs/steps, while worker-enabled startup marks them lost.\n- `packages/gateway-protocol/src/index.test.ts` covers the public durable coordination schemas and validators.\n- `src/gateway/server-methods/durable.test.ts` covers invalid-param rejection before durable state open plus disabled/enabled inspection behavior.\n- `src/durable/recovery.test.ts` and `src/durable/sqlite-store.test.ts` cover the explicit worker gate and future-schema guard.\n\n## Evidence\n\nLatest validation:\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run packages/gateway-protocol/src/index.test.ts`\n  - 1 file, 47 tests passed.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.gateway.config.ts src/gateway/server-methods/durable.test.ts`\n  - 2 files, 6 tests passed.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.unit.config.ts src/durable/startup.test.ts`\n  - 1 file, 2 tests passed.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.unit.config.ts src/durable/recovery.test.ts src/durable/sqlite-store.test.ts src/durable/worker.test.ts src/durable/coordination-projection.test.ts`\n  - 4 files, 24 tests passed.\n- `node scripts/generate-docs-map.mjs --check`\n  - passed with `docs/docs_map.md is up to date`.\n- `npm run tsgo:core`\n  - passed.\n- `git diff --check`\n  - passed.\n\nEarlier post-rebase validation:\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.unit.config.ts src/durable/recovery.test.ts src/durable/sqlite-store.test.ts src/durable/worker.test.ts src/durable/agent-turn.test.ts src/durable/subagent.test.ts src/durable/fan-in.test.ts`\n  - 6 files, 36 tests passed.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.commands.config.ts src/commands/durable.test.ts`\n  - 1 file, 2 tests passed.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.gateway.config.ts src/gateway/server-methods/durable.test.ts`\n  - 2 files, 4 tests passed.\n- `node scripts/generate-docs-map.mjs --check`\n  - passed with `docs/docs_map.md is up to date`.\n- `git diff --check origin/main HEAD`\n  - passed.\n\nLive behavior proof remains in `docs/specs/durable-runtime-foundation-pr-proof-2026-07-01.md` and covers:\n\n- disabled CLI inspection returning the disabled message without creating durable state files;\n- enabled CLI inspection creating/opening `<temp>/state/openclaw.sqlite`;\n- disabled Gateway durable inspection rejecting before opening or migrating durable state;\n- enabled Gateway durable inspection reading a real durable projection from the opt-in shared state DB;\n- gateway startup mark-lost reconciliation gated behind explicit `OPENCLAW_DURABLE_WORKER=1`;\n- invalid durable Gateway params rejected before durable state open.\n\nFull stack typecheck proof is recorded on PR3, which includes this PR2 foundation plus agent/session wiring.\n\n## Notes\n\nThis PR replaces the foundation portion of #97508 with smaller runtime-oriented naming and a narrower review boundary.\n",
